AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_PROFILE=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5
CLASSIFICATION_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.6
MAX_TOOL_ITERATIONS=6
# No API key. Auth is via the standard AWS credential chain (aws configure, env vars,
# or an IAM role) — never commit AWS access keys or secret keys to this file or git.
# AWS_PROFILE is optional — set it to select a named profile from ~/.aws/credentials;
# leave blank to use the default profile / instance role. main.py calls load_dotenv()
# so this (and AWS_REGION) reach boto3 as real process env vars, not just pydantic-settings.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL must be a Bedrock model ID (see AWS Bedrock console -> Model access),
# not a direct-API model name — the two ID formats are different and not interchangeable.
# Verified live: a bare "anthropic.claude-sonnet-5" 400s with "on-demand throughput
# isn't supported" — current-gen models need an inference-profile prefix, e.g.
# "global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5" (no pricing premium, recommended default) or a
# region-scoped one like "eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5" / "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5"
# (~10% premium, use if data residency requires requests to stay in one geography).
